#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119631 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e4f1675-9146-5279-9b64-07a63a9bed99" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative To a Given Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "0a0ea798-5125-5d0e-a755-96bf9af5f543" :question/math-academy-id "e-4823" :question/problem "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ and\n![](images/79/798c2f477907d0d3414eeed0a2f37871c69466d9b4a098699a364f6a034c0679.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}.$ Since we are told that ![](images/de/de91d9b4cd4eabed0a27696d7bf0512c19f6c66eb3c81ab6dc6a73fc0a1c15a5.svg) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(-1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119632 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "841f498b-f737-5086-8f79-44f1a143bebb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "6c7237cd-c655-575f-83ac-7a0891c336b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4824" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/c3/c36abdf2587e3b457ef47d67b3df21d7b8de505202e4bc1f4629e3284c49b87b.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n![](images/e5/e5b57b4f1488c927d64d89cb4352715b471025a111a39fe786c869973401fbd4.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/28/286b19d6c3b5b3fac7f65ffd4adab1b175d4dab5fab1e5bb7a85da692f09224a.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119633 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing More Than Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "90f07e38-405a-5f79-8501-0b4dfb8fa4c8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4825" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\},$ where\n![](images/5d/5d9d3780a503745f072cdb2e9cea0eedddca811143b05a2cc426480e93c8dac9.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/76/766d220a3c5bc2819ab05886751b6a1b782ece06c9d71b9baaaee19e9a2ecbdd.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119674 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2926764-dfbc-5e4e-a6b0-db24a7298a64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis by Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "a79126f2-e26c-5929-93d8-825d85b9a438" :question/math-academy-id "e-6282" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/20/2060371fae8253c2f26c54e53032526c1b1514f282dde33c09657810ed9a6bb7.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n![](images/f7/f778bc04188da8bf824aab34f770f555a01ceabcc0153afd557577f1c8b14414.svg)\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n![](images/cd/cd3c27c4e964d5f4f1f9cf2c1fd5f91c6ba188b58aad1ef9388ba8faf7f03618.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e4f1675-9146-5279-9b64-07a63a9bed99" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative To a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce43d07-7d46-5c98-b744-3a88ad395201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430713} {:answer/id #uuid "b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430721} {:answer/id #uuid "d52b898d-8b0d-5322-b32b-d790188a0c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430724} {:answer/id #uuid "e60504c0-156d-5be5-b8b0-a6c50751ba29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-23 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430726} {:answer/id #uuid "f9aaf9bb-e91f-5b1b-81ad-71ec2b8c9df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430721} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e865a75-dfdd-5a58-b928-640a4073b739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a5b5cd1-19ba-524a-960c-18e8a17d885d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112202" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2926764-dfbc-5e4e-a6b0-db24a7298a64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6641cc50-250b-56ad-b14a-c1124ec8c662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245216} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd41642-b280-5a7c-b432-e2ff0d315b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245311} {:answer/id #uuid "a10427df-c462-55bc-928a-4193f572fa44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245747} {:answer/id #uuid "c751a88a-3aa0-5648-a5b6-305258fb0889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246079} {:answer/id #uuid "dbad1c26-6ccc-544d-abe3-93664ba57768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a10427df-c462-55bc-928a-4193f572fa44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245747} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ec8a63e-d3c0-5582-b9c7-8a8870cbc79b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "438d91ee-b10a-5c27-8e0b-9fc621fd3a05" :question/math-academy-id "q-112208" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=2\\cdot {b}_{1}+3\\cdot {b}_{2}+6\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "841f498b-f737-5086-8f79-44f1a143bebb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82bca19e-14cc-56cc-9397-e33111aae553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430716} {:answer/id #uuid "8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430717} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8f1b4f-ea6f-50a7-90b7-28a18c762dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430718} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f552c7-b78f-5465-9564-878cf6243fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430720} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c9c363-73dc-5320-b19f-2ebf3f0d2405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430717} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d8ec2ef-2c05-5932-bd6d-c9b93200f648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fd80750-80bf-5e1d-b08d-abec51a32d9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112213" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 40\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -10{x}_{2}=40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-4)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "841f498b-f737-5086-8f79-44f1a143bebb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06febdbc-65f9-5901-99f7-6a7827495ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426843} {:answer/id #uuid "5fac1657-f0bf-58cd-839a-2936f55e9617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426846} {:answer/id #uuid "922920ae-5499-5f5e-8c1f-2a7d78b98e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426848} {:answer/id #uuid "a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426849} {:answer/id #uuid "de386f32-9648-5557-95da-e81b5a893cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426849} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbd70cc-1860-587f-a06b-f6be24d7a7e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" :question/math-academy-id "q-112247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(-3)=-7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing More Than Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19420cda-b431-5a47-899b-f28a5a79a06e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317647} {:answer/id #uuid "4894ab4c-1533-51ce-99f5-6fe4ab34c2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317806} {:answer/id #uuid "a99ae0f6-7d7b-5bcf-bdc9-3cee8244b3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318142} {:answer/id #uuid "e58ca5c8-718c-5e6d-b05d-4eeffbd0538a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318331} {:answer/id #uuid "c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430722} :answer-field/id #uuid "e31b6e05-fbe4-51d6-9c76-36484db39779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "127eef35-0ba2-54bf-857c-c0aaa600443a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34764" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 0=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e4f1675-9146-5279-9b64-07a63a9bed99" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative To a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2513b831-2bda-5222-a175-9dbc2cbe0fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-21 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430711} {:answer/id #uuid "29376ce5-1709-5e3d-9b46-93794cef8b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430712} {:answer/id #uuid "54390e6e-dcb1-5dd3-95c7-15b36777dc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430714} {:answer/id #uuid "916a198b-9533-5031-bb1d-8a1a6d13d6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430719} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430723} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5940cf3-d0a0-564c-9b31-70b2bd92b22b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd151813-8e78-53b9-b9c5-57f0cca18b33" :question/math-academy-id "q-35232" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2926764-dfbc-5e4e-a6b0-db24a7298a64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e70132-b4c9-52d8-a99a-a454c18aea30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342570} {:answer/id #uuid "57870f92-6f97-5e07-99ce-3444e70735a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342968} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4f5e5b-d060-5823-a3f2-e785ef7bf05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343001} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0ffb85-7797-55b4-8740-01d2092d531a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343753} {:answer/id #uuid "e12040de-b44a-5701-a813-69e1d45c2701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b4f5e5b-d060-5823-a3f2-e785ef7bf05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343001} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d64fa65-279f-5682-ad6c-973c9785a3ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bf0179e-ce2c-5f32-9679-e1717a127638" :question/math-academy-id "q-75972" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-6)\\cdot {b}_{1}+4\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{1}=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing More Than Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "219502e3-af31-5611-9ead-5045a9c248d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342516} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf985a4-355e-5261-ad9f-710c6c8bed01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342733} {:answer/id #uuid "58c1eed9-7736-5df0-b819-e18f099e18a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342982} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5abdda-188a-520d-bbdf-83d23c0b19b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344313} {:answer/id #uuid "5de78ea6-b293-58dc-961e-a74b7da29c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec5abdda-188a-520d-bbdf-83d23c0b19b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344313} :answer-field/id #uuid "309b2ee3-ef9f-541d-ba25-643af6f67641" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9b1c708-0429-5e44-9bc9-a554cb44ed9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76056" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25 & -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 25{x}_{3}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)-(-1)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$"}]}
